    "modality": "text",
    "language": "en",
    "content": "Biogas plant BGA3 processes mainly slurry and solid substrate. Two solid dosing units (Dos 1 and Dos 2) each feed 50 tonnes of substrate per day directly into fermenters F1 and F2 respectively. Two slurry pre-pits (each 5×8 metres) pump 20 cubic metres of slurry per day into fermenters F1 and F2.\n\nFermenters F1 and F2 each have a diameter of 26 metres and a wall height of 6 metres, each equipped with three paddle agitators. Each fermenter carries a dome roof that also serves as an integrated gas storage. Digestate from F1 and F2 flows into secondary digester N1, which also measures 26 metres in diameter and 6 metres in height and is fitted with one paddle agitator and one long-axis agitator. N1 also has a dome roof as integrated gas storage. From the secondary digester the digestate moves into digestate store G1 with a diameter of 28 metres and a height of 6 metres, equipped with two submersible agitators.\n\nThe biogas produced is fed to a combined heat and power unit (CHP) with a rated electrical output of 500 kW. An emergency flare is available for fault conditions. A condensate shaft is connected to fermenter F1."
  },
